1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,113
This is Asha. Tomorrow, her whole team meets.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:10,698
Charcha translates your words, using your voice with consent.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,120
[Hindi] Hello. Bring twelve blue files to room three at four tomorrow for the meeting.

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,776
Please bring twelve blue files to room 3 at 4 PM for tomorrow's meeting.

5
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:27,382
Room four, not three. Everyone needs the update.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,720
[Telugu] Room four, not room three.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,560
[Punjabi] Room four, not room three.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,855
Ravi confirms. Then Meher. The update needs fresh confirmation.

9
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:48,093
When they leave, the message and confirmations stay together in a bilingual recap.

10
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:54,114
See recorded server timings, alongside experimental AI-voice screening.

11
00:00:55,339 --> 00:01:01,845
That small correction is versioned. Earlier acknowledgements stay with the old version.

12
00:01:02,984 --> 00:01:11,061
Each participant confirms the latest message, and the bilingual recap saves the message and confirmations together.

13
00:01:12,924 --> 00:01:23,701
Behind that exchange, Prisma recognizes speech, Evon translates, and Gnani Timbre speaks. LiveKit carries the call.

14
00:01:24,424 --> 00:01:30,377
People sharing a target language share one branch, with playback kept in order.

15
00:01:31,101 --> 00:01:35,476
Ten language options let each person choose how they listen.

16
00:01:37,566 --> 00:01:40,667
Hosts sign in and admit guests.

17
00:01:42,033 --> 00:01:48,826
The translation GPU warms up for meetings, then scales down after an idle window.

18
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:52,834
Idle time can still be billed.

19
00:01:54,906 --> 00:02:05,144
Two saved cases: 3.94s and 4.23s, translation start to first decoded audio.

20
00:02:05,850 --> 00:02:15,494
Recognition, network, and playback sit outside those measurements. Reports stay available for review after the meeting.

21
00:02:16,628 --> 00:02:22,972
Experimental VoiceShield screens original incoming audio, before any cloned output.

22
00:02:23,399 --> 00:02:29,216
Visible flags or unknown results guide review, without proving identity.

23
00:02:29,644 --> 00:02:33,772
Consented voice cloning preserves the speaker’s voice.

24
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:39,698
Charcha. Different languages. One shared plan.
